# Exemption classes

An exemption is a named class of reason for which an analyzer keeps a symbol the reference graph alone would report. The analyzer names the class in the retained symbol's `retained_by` field, lists the held-back symbols with `print-retained`, and lets `exemptions.disabled` switch a class off by name. This page is generated from `contract/exemptions.json`, which states each class's rule.

